{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1513, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nYou are given an integer array nums of length n.\nA partition is defined as an index i where 0 <= i < n - 1, splitting the array into two non-empty subarrays such that:\n\nLeft subarray contains indices [0, i].\nRight subarray contains indices [i + 1, n - 1].\n\nReturn the number of partitions where the difference between the sum of the left and right subarrays is even.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: nums = [10,10,3,7,6]\nOutput: 4\nExplanation:\nThe 4 partitions are:\n\n[10], [10, 3, 7, 6] with a sum difference of 10 - 26 = -16, which is even.\n[10, 10], [3, 7, 6] with a sum difference of 20 - 16 = 4, which is even.\n[10, 10, 3], [7, 6] with a sum difference of 23 - 13 = 10, which is even.\n[10, 10, 3, 7], [6] with a sum difference of 30 - 6 = 24, which is even.\n\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: nums = [1,2,2]\nOutput: 0\nExplanation:\nNo partition results in an even sum difference.\n\nExample 3:\n\nInput: nums = [2,4,6,8]\nOutput: 3\nExplanation:\nAll partitions result in an even sum difference.\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n2 <= n == nums.length <= 100\n1 <= nums[i] <= 100\n\n### Format: You will use the following starter code to write the solution to the problem and enclose your code within delimiters.\n```python\nclass Solution:\n    def countPartitions(self, nums: List[int]) -> int:\n        \n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1559, "char_start": 1525, "quote": "Input:\n[10, 10, 3, 7, 6]\nOutput:\n4", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 1597, "char_start": 1571, "quote": "Input:\n[1, 2, 2]\nOutput:\n0", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R5", "source": {"char_end": 1638, "char_start": 1609, "quote": "Input:\n[2, 4, 6, 8]\nOutput:\n3", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 3: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "8324eb4908b4fef9df859f58a9ac10606410a309f8ed825dcdfd410bcf0d5871", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "697282c1f5f24f5a78551221bc284542ac3387d5da84a3fe868b941a9857b548", "seq": 2}
